Package: xfce-bluetooth-plugin
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, xfce4-panel, bluez
Recommends: bluez-obexd
Description: Bluetooth manager plugin for the Xfce panel
 Manage Bluetooth from the Xfce panel: turn adapters on and off, pair,
 connect and disconnect devices, rename them, mark them as trusted or
 blocked, and send and receive files.
 .
 File transfer needs the bluez-obexd package, which is recommended but
 not required. Works on X11 and Wayland.
